  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A pump is used to lift a mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> of water from a well to a storage tank at a vertical height <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"h\"></span> in a time interval <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span>. The water is discharged into the tank through a nozzle at a constant speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. Which expression represents the minimum average power delivered to the water by the pump?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mgh}{t}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mv^2}{2t}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{m}{t} \\left( gh + \\frac{1}{2}v^2 \\right)\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{m}{t} (gh + v^2)\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
